  *   If `min <= 0 <= max`: `scale = (max - min) / (2^num_bits - 1) `,
  `min_adj = scale * round(min / scale)` and `max_adj = max + min_adj - min`.

  This operation has a gradient and thus allows for training `min` and `max`
  values.

